  "notes": "Real glyph outlines extracted from public Noto fonts; transparent background; centered in 32x32 tiles. Chronology is approximate script-tradition order (older -> newer from state 15 to state 1), not the age of these modern font outlines or exact individual letter shapes; same-era bands are adjacent, and ties are approximate. Contrast equalized: thin outlines are thickened with a same-colour stroke (strokeWidth, atlas px) and heavy ones dimmed (opacity) so every glyph reaches the same stroke contrast at both display sizes: an 80th-percentile alpha of about 0.89 in the 16 px mip (2x screens) and 0.70 in the 8 px mip (1x screens). States 16 and 17 are the binary glider symbols '0' (Late Babylonian placeholder, traced from Thureau-Dangin 1922) and '1' (a tally incision) from src/lib/life/fonts/oldest-numerals; they sit outside the script chronology."
